James inquired about a quantitative method for identifying an approximate convex hull from a collection of K-D points, looking for terminology linked to scenario or heuristic identification. I initially mentioned various scenario reduction methods but later realized he was referring to **archetypal analysis**. This method identifies a small set of representative archetypes from the data, allowing each original point to be expressed as a convex combination of these archetypes. I clarified that archetypal analysis is often presented alongside PCA, fitting the timeframe James mentioned.
